    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Yep, I wrote it recursively at first. I think it's easier to follow like this.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst resolveSearchParameters = (current: Index): SearchParameters[] => {\r\n  const _resolveSearchParameters = (\r\n    state: SearchParameters[],\r\n    parent: Index | null\r\n  ) => {\r\n    if (parent === null) {\r\n      return state;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return _resolveSearchParameters(\r\n      [parent.getHelper()!.state].concat(state),\r\n      parent.getParent()\r\n    );\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  return _resolveSearchParameters(\r\n    [current.getHelper()!.state],\r\n    current.getParent()\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n```",
